# What does NOT get published to crunchyvfx.com.
#
# Everything listed here is tracked in git because it is part of the project, and none of it belongs
# on the public site. Without this file, `assets.directory: "."` publishes the WHOLE REPO — the
# design document, the working notes, the test suite, the Tauri and Flatpak sources — on every path
# a crawler can find. Same file, same reason, as CrunchyBGM's.
#
# The published set is deliberately small: index.html, the fifteen sibling scripts (suite.js 2026-10-09, crunchy-icons.js
# 2026-10-11; project.js left and project-app.js, plant.js, library.js, settings.js, desktop.js joined with VFX-DESIGN §18;
# feedback.js with §20; glyphs.js with §28), the two stylesheets (crunchy-base.css, styles.css), and the
# three images (favicon, apple-touch-icon, og), plus about.html (the web's About page, served at /about),
# robots.txt, sitemap.xml and the IndexNow key <32 hex>.txt for search engines (VFX-DESIGN §29; tests/seo.test.mjs checks none is matched),
# and version.json, what the desktop app's update check reads (§30; tests/worker.test.mjs checks it is not matched). If you add a file the APP loads at runtime, it must
# NOT be matched here — check DEPLOY.md's checklist after adding one.
*.md
tests/
tools/
scripts/
src-tauri/
flatpak/
dist/
.vscode/
.claude/
.github/
.gitattributes
.githooks/
.wrangler/
wrangler.jsonc
worker.js
.assetsignore
synth-manifest.json
*.aseprite
*.crunchyvfx
